        type: "paragraph",
        text: "PPC ads for law firms, most commonly run through Google Ads, place a firm's listing at the top of search results for chosen keywords, with the firm paying only when someone clicks the ad. Legal keywords are among the most expensive in any industry, sometimes reaching costs well into the hundreds of dollars per click for competitive personal injury and criminal defense terms in major metro markets, which makes campaign management discipline essential rather than optional. Effective legal PPC depends heavily on tight keyword targeting, negative keywords that filter out irrelevant searches, dedicated landing pages built around a specific offer rather than sending traffic to a general homepage, and continuous monitoring of which keywords and ad variations actually produce signed cases rather than just clicks.",
