        type: "paragraph",
        text: "Firms that get this wrong don't necessarily do so through bad intent; it's often simply a matter of using a payment processor not built with this distinction in mind, where fees are automatically deducted from the deposit before it ever reaches the account, without the firm actively choosing that structure. This is precisely the kind of error that a bar disciplinary review can flag even when the underlying dollar amounts are small and no client was actually harmed, since the violation is technical and procedural rather than dependent on provable harm.",
